{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement each user story as an independent Spring Boot / Spring Integration module following the source/sink module model (analogous to Spring Cloud Stream app starters), packaged as a standalone executable jar with externalized configuration properties and configuration-metadata.",
    "Target Java 17+ and Spring Framework 6 / Spring Boot 3, per the specification's baseline requirements.",
    "U1 WebSocket source is built on the existing Spring Integration WebSocket support (server-side inbound WebSocket channel adapter), not a from-scratch WebSocket server.",
    "U2 AWS source and U4 AWS sink are built on the Spring Integration AWS extension: S3 inbound adapter (polling/streaming) plus SES ingestion via SNS/SQS notification pipeline; S3 sink via the S3 message handler with configurable key-naming and multipart upload.",
    "U3 Cassandra sink uses the DataStax Java driver / Spring Data Cassandra with configurable keyspace, table mapping, consistency level and batching.",
    "U5 HAWQ sink writes files to HDFS in Avro/Parquet format and registers/provisions PXF external tables so HAWQ can read them; PXF DDL generation is part of the module.",
    "U6 SOLR sink uses SolrJ with configurable collection, field mapping and commit strategy.",
    "U7 is implemented as shared error-handling infrastructure usable by every module: a configurable global error channel (default binding named like 'topic.errors.stream.module'), a configurable catch pattern (default '**Exception'), an exception hierarchy (GlobalException -> DefaultException / ModuleSpecificException), and an error-message enricher that traverses the exception chain to preserve the root 'Caused by:' and stages the error as the channel payload while ingestion continues.",
    "A single Maven multi-module build with a shared parent POM, common module archetype, and CI pipeline (build, unit tests, integration tests) is set up once and reused by all modules.",
    "Integration tests use Testcontainers/LocalStack (AWS), embedded/Testcontainers Cassandra, and embedded Solr; U5 uses a dedicated Hadoop/HAWQ test environment.",
    "U8 requires no new production code (feature already in GA); the effort covers designing and executing regression/scaling tests that add and remove modules while verifying partition-strategy state is preserved."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer performs all work; all figures are effort (work-hours), not elapsed calendar time.",
    "The referenced Spring Integration WebSocket support and Spring Integration AWS extension are reused as libraries; the work is building and packaging the source/sink modules around them, not reimplementing the extensions.",
    "The underlying stream runtime/deployment platform already exists (GA) and provides module deployment, binding and partitioning infrastructure; only U8's testing effort is in scope for that area.",
    "Sandbox accounts/environments are available for testing: AWS (or LocalStack), a Cassandra cluster, a Solr server, and a Hadoop/HAWQ cluster with PXF for U5 integration tests.",
    "No user interface work is required; modules are configured purely through properties/YAML.",
    "Documentation scope is limited to per-module READMEs, configuration-property metadata and a short aggregated reference section.",
    "The developer is experienced with Spring Integration; the only significant learning curve is HAWQ/PXF specifics for U5, which is reflected in its higher estimate.",
    "Per-module estimates include unit tests; integration/E2E testing that spans multiple modules is estimated separately.",
    "Requirements are stable; no rework due to changing requirements is included."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and solution architecture",
      "activity_description": "Analyze U1-U8, define module contracts (source/sink interfaces, payload formats, property namespaces), error-handling architecture, and produce the overall design for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Project scaffolding, build and CI setup",
      "activity_description": "Create Maven multi-module project, shared parent POM, module archetype, dependency management, configuration-metadata generation, and CI pipeline (compile, unit test, integration test stages).",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U1 WebSocket source module - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the WebSocket source module using Spring Integration WebSocket support: server endpoint, inbound channel adapter wiring, message mapping of browser events, and configuration properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U1 WebSocket source module - testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests and integration tests with a WebSocket client simulating browser sessions, covering connect/disconnect, message ingestion and error paths.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U2 AWS source module (S3, SES) - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the AWS source using the Spring Integration AWS extension: S3 inbound adapter (polling/streaming of new objects) and SES ingestion via SNS/SQS notification pipeline, with credential/region configuration properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U2 AWS source module - testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests and LocalStack/Testcontainers-based integration tests for S3 ingestion and the SES notification flow.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U3 Cassandra sink module - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Cassandra sink message handler: connection/session management, configurable keyspace/table and field mapping, consistency level, batching and high-throughput write tuning.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U3 Cassandra sink module - testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests plus integration tests against an embedded/Testcontainers Cassandra instance, including throughput-oriented write scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U4 AWS sink module (S3) - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the S3 sink message handler: bucket/key naming strategy (SpEL-driven), content-type handling, multipart upload for large payloads, and retry/ACL configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U4 AWS sink module - testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests and LocalStack-based integration tests verifying object creation, key naming, metadata and failure handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U5 HAWQ sink module - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the HAWQ sink: write data files to HDFS in Avro/Parquet format, generate/execute PXF external table DDL, manage file rollover and partitioning, and expose configuration properties.",
      "most_likely_effort": 56
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "U5 HAWQ sink module - testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests plus integration tests against a Hadoop/HAWQ test environment validating Avro/Parquet output and PXF external table readability.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "U6 SOLR sink module - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the SOLR sink using SolrJ: configurable collection/core, field mapping, document conversion, commit/soft-commit strategy and batching for full-text indexing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "U6 SOLR sink module - testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests and integration tests against an embedded/standalone Solr server, verifying indexing, searchability and commit behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "U7 Error channel infrastructure - implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement global error channel support: configurable error channel binding (e.g., 'topic.errors.stream.module'), configurable catch pattern (e.g., 'catch=**Exception'), exception hierarchy (GlobalException -> DefaultException -> ModuleSpecificException), and error-message enrichment that traverses the exception chain to preserve the root 'Caused by:' as the staged payload while ingestion continues.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "U7 Error channel infrastructure - testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit and integration tests covering failures at source, processor and sink modules (custom and built-in), cause-chain traversal, payload staging and routing to the error channel.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "U8 Partition strategy state preservation - testing",
      "activity_description": "Design and execute regression tests that dynamically add and delete modules/partitions and verify the partition strategy state is preserved and modules adapt correctly (testing effort only; feature already in GA).",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "Cross-module end-to-end integration testing",
      "activity_description": "End-to-end stream tests combining sources and sinks (e.g., WebSocket->Cassandra, AWS S3->SOLR, HTTP source with error channel routing per U7 scenario) across the deployed modules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Per-module READMEs, configuration property reference, error-channel configuration guide (U7) and aggregated reference documentation for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "Release packaging and verification",
      "activity_description": "Versioning, building releasable artifacts (jars), publishing module metadata, and smoke-verifying deployment of each module in the runtime.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 616
  }
}

